    'work.genie-platform.step.1.title': 'Map information flows first',
    'work.genie-platform.step.1.desc': 'Spent the first weeks understanding how intelligence actually moved in client organisations what was the daily workflow of an analyst, what did an engagement manager need before a major meeting. These conversations revealed the gaps and shaped every subsequent design decision.',
    'work.genie-platform.step.2.title': 'Design navigation before any feature',
    'work.genie-platform.step.2.desc': 'Getting the navigation right meant users could find things predictably and move between related areas without losing context. The left nav became a consistent anchor point, with key sections always accessible regardless of which feature area you were in.',
    'work.genie-platform.step.3.title': 'Build the design system in parallel, not after',
    'work.genie-platform.step.3.desc': 'GENIE DS was built alongside feature work rather than as a separate project. Every component designed for a specific feature was abstracted into the system at the same time so the system reflected real usage patterns rather than theoretical ones.',
    'work.genie-platform.step.4.title': 'Design Ask Genie as part of every workflow',
    'work.genie-platform.step.4.desc': 'Ask Genie is available on the stakeholder profile, accessible from the media feed, embedded in the dashboard, present in the network view. It appears contextually when there\'s relevant intelligence to surface, it surfaces it; when there isn\'t, it stays out of the way.',

